The Polisher, Grinder, Cleaning Sponge, and Spray Paint work on a small area at a time, so a whole vehicle takes many passes. Turn the mouse wheel to make the brush up to 5 times wider, and a ring on the surface shows how big it is.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Brush size on the mouse wheel or gamepad[/b]: snap the Polisher, Grinder, or Cleaning Sponge to a surface and turn the mouse wheel or press LB and RB on a gamepad to resize the brush, up to 5x. With no tool snapped, the wheel changes the hotbar as usual.[/*]
[*][b]Brush preview[/b]: while the tool is snapped, a ring on the surface shows the brush size, in the same style as the Spray Paint ring.[/*]
[*][b]Bigger Spray Paint brush[/b]: the Spray Paint keeps the game's Brush Size control and gets extra sizes above its largest one, up to 4x with the default settings (8x with a max size of 10).[/*]
[*][b]Pay for the work, not the time[/b]: the Polisher, Grinder, and Spray Paint drain only for surface they change, at half the game's cost by default. Finished surface cost nothing.[/*]
[*][b]Limits[/b]: a brush radius never goes above 2 m, the game's own limit. With a max size above 5, some tools stop before it: the Polisher at about 8.9x, the Cleaning Sponge at about 6.7x.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Multiplayer[/b][/size]
Not tested in co-op. The bigger brush should work for each player who installs the mod. The drain rules and the extra Spray Paint sizes need the mod on the host.

[size=4][b]Save safety[/b][/size]
The mod stores nothing in your save, so you can remove it at any time.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Nomad Drive 1.0 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nomaddrive/mods/7]Nomad Drive BepInEx Pack[/url].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/nomaddrive/mods/7]BepInEx pack[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Nomad Drive\BepInEx\plugins\RestorationToolsTweaks.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]RestorationToolsTweaks.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.nomaddrive.restorationtoolstweaks.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-nd/nd-restoration-tools-tweaks/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

